---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About">
  <div style="max-width:640px">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Home</a>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,2.6rem);font-weight:400;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:24px;line-height:1.15">
      Built this for me,<br><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--accent)">but you can read it too.</em>
    </h1>

    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        I'm Anthony Catanese — product manager, builder, occasional writer. I've been putting things on the internet since around 2006, across a handful of domains and more WordPress installs than I care to count.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each time, I'd try something, restart, and lose the thread. This time the plan is different: the experiments <em>are</em> the content. I build small things with AI, ship them publicly, and write honestly about how it went — the wrong turns included.
      </p>
      <p>
        The blog has 20 years of posts on it: product management, observations, reviews, travel stories, and whatever I was thinking about at the time. It's all here.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want to follow along, you can reach me at <a href="mailto:ranthonycatanese@gmail.com">ranthonycatanese@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
